Spec: Render

Purpose:
  Encode the post the person saved.

Owns:
  ./render.rs

Must:
  Read plan.json and ignore the terminal.
  Cut each card with ffmpeg, scale and pad to the post frame, and write H.264 post.mp4 with the source audio.
  Write post.jpg for a photo card.
  Write slice.txt and caption.txt from the plan.
  slice.txt records source, start, end, and the person's note, or the source and times when the note is empty.
  A Reel is one card. A Story is one to five. A carousel is two to ten.
  A Story card and a carousel video slide are at most 60 seconds.
  A Reel is as long as its moment, within the length Instagram accepts.
  Stories and Reels are 9:16. Every carousel slide uses the first slide's frame.

Must not:
  Call the network.
  Draw the terminal.
  Mark a post chosen.
  Join unrelated clips into one post.

Scenario: save encodes one post
  Given plan.json describes one Reel card from a source video
  When render runs
  Then post.mp4 is H.264 and keeps the source audio
  And slice.txt names that source and its start and end
